5️⃣ union()

set1 = {1, 2, 3}
set2 = {3, 4, 5}

print(set1.union(set2))

Output

{1, 2, 3, 4, 5}


---

6️⃣ intersection()

set1 = {1, 2, 3}
set2 = {2, 3, 4}

print(set1.intersection(set2))

Output

{2, 3}


---

7️⃣ difference()

set1 = {1, 2, 3}
set2 = {2, 3, 4}

print(set1.difference(set2))

Output

{1}

🌍 Real-World Example

python_students = {"Veshma", "Rahul", "Priya"}
sql_students = {"Priya", "Rahul", "Kiran"}

common_students = python_students.intersection(sql_students)

print(common_students)

Output

{'Rahul', 'Priya'}

 Key Learning

add() → Adds one element.

update() → Adds multiple elements.

remove() → Removes an element (raises an error if not found).

discard() → Removes an element without raising an error.

pop() → Removes a random element.

clear() → Removes all elements.

union() → Combines two sets.

intersection() → Finds common elements.

difference() → Finds elements present only in the first set.


